  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale\nThe central idea is to use a physics-informed neural network (PINN) approach combined with physics-informed constraints to parameterize the step function h(x). The PINN architecture enforces the integral constraint and bounds automatically through its initialization and operations. This is inspired by the observation that the mother function for scattering transforms is used in harmonic analysis, and the constraints can be naturally embedded using activation functions and scaling.\n\nThe rationale is that by embedding constraints directly into the network architecture and optimization process, we can escape local optima and achieve globally better solutions. We hypothesize that this approach will find superior solutions by maintaining validity throughout optimization cycles.\n\n2. Mathematical Specification\nWe represent h(x) as a periodic piecewise linear function parameterized by:\n  - Amplitudes (a_i) and phases (\u03c6_i)\n  - Frequencies (\u03c9_i)\n  - Duration coefficients (t_i)\n\nThe function is constructed as:\n  h(x) = (1/n) * \u2211_{i=1}^{M} t_i * sin(\u03c9_i * x + \u03c6_i)\n\nWhere the constraint is automatically enforced by summing over x dx:\n\n  \u222b_0^2 h(x) dx = (2/n) * \u2211_{i=1}^{M} t_i/n * [ -cos(\u03c9_i*x + \u03c6_i)/(\u03c9_i) ]_0^2 * (2) = (4/n) * \u2211_{i=1}^{M} t_i/n * [ sin(\u03c9_i*\u03c6_i) - sin(\u03c9_i*(\u03c6_i+2\u03c0)) ] = 0\n\nHowever, to maintain 0\u2264h(x)\u22641, we use scaled activation functions. The optimization minimizes a penalized version of the correlation objective.\n\n3. Implementation Procedure\n- For n=256 points, initialize neural network parameters (amplitudes, phases, frequencies, durations)\n- Use Adam optimizer with 100 iterations, incorporating gradient projection for bounds\n- Evaluate correlation over all lags using direct numerical integration\n- Compute loss as max_edge (maximum correlation)\n- Update parameters to minimize max_edge\n\n4. Search Choices and Useful Variations\n- Layer structure: piecewise linear with periodic activation\n- Initialization: random within valid domain\n- Optimization environment: Adam with fixed step size\n- Loss function: max correlation penalized twice for reliability\n- Hyperparameter search:\n\n  \ud83d\udd12 A",
